From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:07:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] chre: do not start the msm daemon automatically

On a device where the daemon cannot reach the SLPI it exits non-zero
about 33 times a boot. init counts the 5th bad exit before
sys.boot_completed, sets sys.init.updatable_crashing, and apexd answers
that by reverting and rebooting -- a boot loop whose cause is three
services away from the symptom.

'disabled' keeps init from starting it, 'oneshot' keeps init from
restarting it when it is started by hand, so neither route reaches that
counter and the daemon can be tested on a booted device instead of
costing a reboot to find out.

Drop both lines on a device where the DSP side works.
---
 host/msm/chre_daemon_msm.rc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/host/msm/chre_daemon_msm.rc b/host/msm/chre_daemon_msm.rc
index 5de25525f..dfb4c59a7 100644
--- a/host/msm/chre_daemon_msm.rc
+++ b/host/msm/chre_daemon_msm.rc
@@ -19,6 +19,13 @@ on post-fs-data
 
 service vendor.chre /vendor/bin/chre_daemon_msm
     class late_start
+    # Not started at boot on this device. The daemon cannot open a fastrpc session to the SLPI and
+    # exits non-zero ~33 times a boot; the 5th bad exit before sys.boot_completed sets
+    # sys.init.updatable_crashing, and apexd answers that by reverting and rebooting. disabled
+    # keeps init from starting it, oneshot keeps init from restarting it if it is started by hand,
+    # so neither path can reach that counter. Drop both once the DSP side works.
+    disabled
+    oneshot
     user context_hub
     group wakelock context_hub
     capabilities BLOCK_SUSPEND
